event: response.output_text.done
data: {"sequence_number": 235, "type": "response.output_text.done", "content_index": 0, "item_id": "msg_05df5097-f2ef-994b-8aee-1949580e1c71", "output_index": 8, "text": "The latest stable Rust release is **1.99.1**, released on **October 15, 2026**.\n\nIt is a point release that fixes regressions from 1.99.0 (released October 1, 2026), including a missing `wcslen` symbol on some targets, an FFI `bool` return miscompilation on x86_64, and a `rust-lld` library-loading issue on macOS. Sources: the [official announcement](https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/15/Rust-1.99.1/), the [Rust releases index](https://blog.rust-lang.org/releases/), [GitHub tags](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/tags), and trackers such as [releases.rs](https://releases.rs/) and [endoflife.date](https://endoflife.date/rust). [[1]](https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/15/Rust-1.99.1/) [[2]](https://blog.rust-lang.org/releases/) [[3]](https://releases.rs/) [[4]](https://endoflife.date/rust)", "logprobs": []}

